# Claude Desktop instances.
#
#   name | bundle id | profile dir | icon hue (degrees) | env (optional)
#
# env        subscription mode: only CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR=path is supported.
#            Leading ~ is expanded as data. Provider/API keys, endpoint, proxy
#            and runtime overrides are rejected. Never put tokens here.
#            The child starts with a minimal environment. Code's own shell,
#            project, local and managed settings can still add configuration.
#
# name       ASCII letter followed by letters/digits/hyphen/underscore, max 64;
#            becomes the app "/Applications/Claude <name>.app" and its selector
#            (lowercased) for claude-apps-refresh.sh
# bundle id  must be unique per instance; changing it later forces a re-login
# profile    each instance MUST have its own; two instances sharing one profile
#            can corrupt it
# hue        0 red · 30 orange · 55 yellow · 142 green · 175 teal · 212 blue
#            · 275 purple · 320 pink   (icon is generated on first build)
#
# Add a line, run `claude-apps-refresh.sh`, and the new instance is built.
# Keep this file inside your home, owned by you, with no group/other write
# permissions or custom allow ACLs on it or its ancestors. Do not run with sudo.
# Desktop and Code paths cannot overlap, including ancestor/descendant or case
# aliases. Supported legacy paths are flat, printable-ASCII Claude/Claude-*
# directories in ~/Library/Application Support and ~/.claude/.claude-* for Code.
# Arbitrary home/system directories, writable ancestors and custom allow ACLs
# are refused. Missing CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR means ~/.claude (one instance only).
# --list prints variable names only. The launcher refuses all caller arguments
# and refuses inherited proxy variables instead of silently bypassing a proxy.
#
# New profiles can use managed UUID paths (generate a fresh ID for each):
# ~/Library/Application Support/Multi Claude Desktop/Profiles/<UUID>/desktop
# ~/Library/Application Support/Multi Claude Desktop/Profiles/<UUID>/code
# Existing histories are not moved or copied automatically.

Personal   | com.example.claude-personal   | ~/Library/Application Support/Claude            | 142 |
Enterprise | com.example.claude-enterprise | ~/Library/Application Support/Claude-Enterprise | 212 | CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR=~/.claude-work
